<%#
  A player in a column, so two of them stand side by side on a phone.

  Same devices as the row: his club's colour, the badge behind him, and the grade on
  the card's own white with the colour cut away from it at the lean the logo is cut
  at. What differs is the axis — the row cuts a vertical edge, this cuts a horizontal
  one — and where he stands: beside his name where there is room, under it where
  there is not.
%>
<div class="flex h-[200px] flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 bg-white shadow-sm sm:h-[168px]">
  <%# 20px across the card's width is the logo's lean, read the other way round. %>
  <%# From sm he stands beside his name, so the name is set against him rather than
      pinned to the top: centred on the block, less the slant the block loses at the
      bottom, so it reads as centred on what you can actually see. %>
  <div class="relative flex-1 overflow-hidden [clip-path:polygon(0_0,100%_0,100%_calc(100%_-_20px),0_100%)] sm:flex sm:items-center sm:pb-3 <%= text_class %>"
       style="background-color: <%= color %>">

    <%# The badge is centred on the cutout's box, not the card's, so it reads as
        something he is standing in front of. The outer span traces that box: same
        corner, same height, and the ratio the Premier League serves its photos at,
        so the centring holds even when there is no cutout to stand there.

        He stands on the slant: his feet are the region's own bottom edge, so the cut
        runs across him and there is no band of bare colour left underneath. The clip
        on the region is what stops him spilling onto the white below it.

        Below sm he stands under his name; from sm up he stands beside it. %>
    <span class="pointer-events-none absolute bottom-0 left-1/2 z-0 aspect-[219/280] h-[92px] -translate-x-1/2 sm:left-auto sm:right-0 sm:h-[104px] sm:translate-x-0">
      <% if team&.badge_url %>
        <span class="absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 h-[104px] w-[104px] -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 sm:h-[118px] sm:w-[118px]">
          <%= image_tag team.badge_url, alt: "", class: "h-full w-full object-contain opacity-20 #{badge_silhouette}" %>
        </span>
        <span class="absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 h-[104px] w-[104px] -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 sm:h-[118px] sm:w-[118px]">
          <%= image_tag team.badge_url, alt: "", class: "h-full w-full object-contain opacity-[.22]" %>
        </span>
      <% end %>

      <% if player.cutout_url %>
        <%= image_tag player.cutout_url, alt: "",
              class: "absolute bottom-0 left-1/2 block h-full w-auto -translate-x-1/2 object-bottom drop-shadow-[0_5px_9px_rgba(0,0,0,0.24)]",
              onerror: "this.remove()" %>
      <% end %>
    </span>

    <%# His name sits over the colour beside him, as it does on the row and the hero.
        The right padding only exists from sm, because below it he is not there. %>
    <div class="relative z-[1] min-w-0 px-2.5 pt-2.5 sm:w-full sm:pt-0 sm:pr-[84px]">
      <% if player.given_name.present? %>
        <p class="truncate text-[9.5px] font-bold uppercase leading-none tracking-[-0.02em] opacity-80"><%= player.given_name %></p>
      <% end %>
      <p class="mt-[3px] truncate text-[17px] font-extrabold uppercase leading-none tracking-[-0.02em] sm:text-[19px]">
        <%= player.display_name %><% if captain? %><span class="ml-[5px] align-top text-[11px] opacity-90">(C)</span><% end %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-[5px] flex items-center gap-x-1 truncate text-[10px] font-bold leading-none opacity-95">
        <span><%= team&.short_name %></span>
        <% if cost %>
          <span class="font-normal opacity-50">/</span><span class="tabular-nums"><%= cost %></span>
        <% end %>
        <% if ownership %>
          <span class="font-normal opacity-50">/</span><span class="tabular-nums"><%= ownership %></span>
        <% end %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# The white the colour was cut away from. The grade stands on it, as it does at
      the end of a row. %>
  <%# The slant leaves a wedge of white deepest at the right, which is where the
      grade stands, so it is set to the height of that wedge rather than to the
      points beside it. %>
  <div class="flex shrink-0 items-baseline justify-between px-2.5 pb-1.5 text-zinc-900">
    <p class="text-[20px] font-extrabold leading-none tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums"><%= headline if headline? %></p>
    <p class="text-[38px] font-extrabold leading-none tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-[42px]"><%= grade %></p>
  </div>
</div>
